    "Notes Updated": "10/10/2024",
    "Scouting Notes": "Starter or Reliever\n Made the move to the rotation in May, and just dominated all year\n Whiff rate of 37.5% overall was 97th percentile for pitchers with at least 40 IP in 2024\n ERA was 96th percentile, FIP was 99th\n Fastball is a solid shape, sitting around 93 and averaging 18\" of IVB, along with a  4.5 VAA, it will play and especially will play up in the zone or above\n His 85 mph bullet slider grades out the best of all of them. 48% whiff rate, 40% chase rate, 31% ball rate and 58% CSW%\n Curve is a big breaker, with sharp movement downward, but some sweep as well\n Cutter is a really solid ptich in the 86 88 range\n Changeup is a similar velo to the cutter, made big strides this year going from poor to average ish",
    "Notes Updated 2": "1/12/2024",
    "Scouting Notes 2": "Likely a reliever, but did start in college\n Drafted by Pirates in Round 12 in 2022 but didn't sign\n Fastball has shown some solid ride at times, sink at other times. Inconsistent in college but showed some decent flashes\n Slider is a plus pitch, mid 80's and firm. Can land in zone and get chase.\n Curve is another really solid secondary. Mid upper 70s, high spin.\n Rarely used changeup\n Walks not a huge issue, but needs to command fastball better, below avg command overall\n Really solid UDFA pick up. I like Hunt quite a bit. Hopefully in A ball to start next year and see where it goes from there.",
